<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Relationships whose REFERENCED (one-side) table is rev_provider. WBS 0.4 remainder.

  THE FILE NAME IS NOT A FREE CHOICE - same packer mechanics as every other file in this
  folder (see Other/Relationships/rev_applicant.xml's own header for the full explanation of
  EntityRelationshipProcessor's file-per-referenced-entity grouping). All three children below
  are grouped here because all three are referenced-side rev_provider.

  ALL THREE ARE "REFERENTIAL, RESTRICT DELETE" - AND THAT IS A DIFFERENT CASCADE PROFILE FROM
  EVERY OTHER RELATIONSHIP IN THIS SOLUTION SO FAR. Every relationship declared before this
  file is either Parental/Cascade (the Applicant/Application/Grant/Review retention spine) or
  the Referential/RemoveLink pattern Get-RevSyntheticRelationship uses for the systemuser
  lookups. Restrict Delete is a THIRD profile: TAD section 3.3 states plainly "Provider
  survives; cannot be deleted while grants reference it" - that is stronger than RemoveLink
  (which lets the parent be deleted and just nulls the child's lookup): it must BLOCK deletion
  of the Provider row outright while any Bank Account, Grant or Payment row still references
  it. Reference data must not disappear from historical financial records (TAD section 3.3's
  own "why" column).

  CascadeDelete=Restrict IS AN UNVERIFIED PLATFORM CONTRACT (E2, NOT E1) - A-FIN-01 IN THE
  DEV SUMMARY UNVALIDATED ASSUMPTIONS REGISTER (docs/development/revitalise-grant-automation-
  dev-summary.md, "WBS 0.4 remainder" revision). No relationship anywhere in this solution has used any CascadeDelete
  value other than Cascade (the parental spine) or RemoveLink
  (Get-RevSyntheticRelationship's systemuser lookups) before this file, so "Restrict" as the
  customizations.xml / Web API CascadeConfiguration.Delete value for the maker portal's own
  "Referential, Restrict Delete" behaviour preset has NOT been ground-truthed against a live
  environment in this repository (no environment write is available to this session -
  IMP-0084/IMP-0133). It is asserted here from general Dataverse platform knowledge (the
  CascadeType enum's documented members: NoCascade, Cascade, RemoveLink, Restrict, Active,
  UserOwned), not from an export+unpack of a real instance the way IMP-0001 requires. Cheapest
  verification: create one of these three relationships via the Web API against DEV once an
  environment is available, then GET it back and confirm CascadeConfiguration.Delete reads
  "Restrict" and that a delete of the Provider row while a referencing row exists is actually
  rejected by the platform - see Dev Summary Unvalidated Assumptions Register.

  The other four cascade behaviours (Assign/Reparent/Share/Unshare) are set to NoCascade for
  all three, matching the maker portal's own "Referential, Restrict Delete" preset and the
  precedent Get-RevSyntheticRelationship's header already documents for the plain
  "Referential" preset it uses (NoCascade on those same four, RemoveLink instead of Restrict
  on Delete only).
-->
